[line]
[size=4][b]A FEW HIGHLIGHTS[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]LIGHTING[/b][/size]

PIXL combines screen-space lighting with persistent world-space lighting, expanded local lights, ambient sky response, contact shadows and atmospheric lighting. Dark areas receive more believable bounce light while fires, windows, magic and other local lights contribute more naturally.

[img width=735]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789146469-368979845.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]MATERIALS & TERRAIN[/b][/size]

Stone should look like stone. Metal should look like metal. Wet wood should not look like dry wood. PIXL expands roughness, metallic response, parallax, clearcoat, micro-detail and terrain blending while retaining normal Skyrim content. Supported terrain can deform under actors; parallax enhances relief without changing collision.

[img width=721]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789150098-1630591381.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]CHARACTERS[/b][/size]

Characters have dedicated skin, hair and translucent-material rendering rather than using the same response as the environment.

[img width=716]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789148543-1629008285.png[/img]
[i]Vanilla textures, Neural Rendering disabled, skin shading with micro-detail.[/i]

[size=4][b]VEGETATION[/b][/size]

Grass and foliage receive improved lighting, transmission and material response so vegetation fits the scene instead of glowing or looking plasticky.

[img width=832]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789146556-1115423108.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]WATER[/b][/size]

Improved surface lighting, water optics, caustics, underwater rendering and distant-water transitions.

[img width=824]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789149350-1086728168.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]WEATHER AND WORLD RESPONSE[/b][/size]

Rain responds through wet materials, puddles, splashes, mist, wind and persistent world-space roof runoff. Heavy rain reduces long-range visibility and shifts the atmosphere toward a darker storm mood. Snow and mud can react to actors and retain deformation in the world.

Atmospheric fog responds to weather and time of day, with controls for balancing depth, height and sky visibility.

Snow and mud can also react to actors instead of always behaving like completely flat textures.

[img width=594]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789148614-1973565112.jpg[/img]
[img width=593]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789148834-967665520.png[/img]
[img width=593]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789148814-1287672311.png[/img]
[img width=456]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789444570-707901596.gif[/img]

[size=4][b]WINDOW LIFE[/b][/size]

Supported windows can gain simulated depth, day/night scenery, glass refraction and optional room details such as curtains, furniture and moving silhouettes. Results depend on the source material, so the controls allow conservative tuning.

It's an illusion rather than a fully rendered room, and results depend on the window material. The controls let you dial it back where an asset doesn't cooperate.

It's a small effect, but it's one of my favourites.

[img width=491]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789149811-184882514.gif[/img]
[img width=487]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789149410-1454604861.png[/img]

[line]
[size=4][b]DLSS / DLAA / FSR / FRAME GENERATION[/b][/size]

PIXL includes integration work around modern reconstruction and frame-generation technologies.

[b]Quick Setup offers:[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Off[/b]  native rendering without temporal reconstruction.[/*]
[*][b]TAA[/b]  native-resolution temporal anti-aliasing.[/*]
[*][b]FSR Quality[/b]  lower-resolution rendering reconstructed to your output resolution.[/*]
[*][b]DLSS Quality[/b]  NVIDIA reconstruction on supported hardware.[/*]
[*][b]DLAA[/b]  native-resolution DLSS anti-aliasing, without an upscaling performance boost.[/*]
[/list]

DLSS and DLAA are unavailable when the required hardware/runtime support is not detected.

You can also enable frame generation during setup. [b]Frame generation and the optional Neural Rendering path require borderless/windowed mode.[/b] If PIXL asks for a restart, save your game and relaunch through your usual SKSE or mod-manager shortcut.

Frame generation improves displayed smoothness; it does not increase the game's simulation or input-update rate.

[color=#ff0000]DLSS5/Frame Gen requires borderless/windowed mode, it will currently NOT work in Fullscreen. Please edit your SkyrimPrefs.ini and ensure bFull Screen=0 is set.[/color]

The optional DLSSG proxy is not bundled. Follow its upstream instructions and install only one proxy beside SkyrimSE.exe. These paths remain experimental and hardware-specific issues are possible.

[b]Optional DLSSG proxy[/b]

The third-party [url=https://github.com/sdli1995/dlssg_for_sm86]DLSSG proxy[/url] is [b]not bundled[/b] with PIXL. It is not required for ordinary DLSS/DLAA or FSR frame generation.

For a compatible proxy setup, follow the [url=https://github.com/sdli1995/dlssg_for_sm86/blob/main/README.en.md]upstream installation instructions[/url]. Its proxy DLL and [b]dlssg_sm86.ini[/b] belong beside [b]SkyrimSE.exe[/b], not inside Data.

[b]Do not overwrite another mod's proxy DLL.[/b] Use only an upstream-supported alternative entry point if appropriate, and install only one proxy from that project.

After installation, relaunch Skyrim, select the DLSSG backend in PIXL's Camera controls and enable frame generation. A further restart may be required to create the presentation sidecar.

PIXL greys out DLSSG when neither native support nor the expected proxy files are detected. Detecting files is not a guarantee of compatibility.

[color=#f1c232]The optional DLSSG proxy and Neural Rendering paths remain experimental. Hardware-specific issues are possible; use the standard reconstruction and FSR frame-generation options if those paths are unavailable or unstable.[/color]

[b]Credit where it's due[/b]

A lot of the groundwork for getting these technologies into Skyrim exists because other modders did the difficult work first.

Special credit goes to PureDark's Skyrim Upscaler, which brought DLSS, DLAA, FSR2 and XeSS into Skyrim through SKSE.

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/80343]Skyrim Upscaler  DLSS / FSR2 / XeSS by PureDark[/url]

The Community Shaders frame-generation work by [b]doodlum, PureDark and Flayan[/b] also provided important prior work around FSR 3.1 Frame Generation, NVIDIA Streamline and Skyrim's rendering pipeline.

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/140199]Frame Generation  Community Shaders legacy module[/url]

These links acknowledge prior work; they are not instructions to install another upscaler or renderer alongside PIXL.

PIXL also uses technology from [b]NVIDIA Streamline[/b] and [b]AMD FidelityFX[/b] where applicable.

[url=https://github.com/NVIDIA-RTX/Streamline]NVIDIA Streamline[/url]
[url=https://github.com/GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/FidelityFX-SDK]AMD FidelityFX SDK[/url]

Full licensing, third-party notices and code provenance are included with the project and source.

[line]
[size=4][b]REQUIREMENTS[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition on a supported Windows runtime[/*]
[*]SKSE and Engine Fixes matching that runtime[/*]
[*]PIXL-TerrainField.esp enabled[/*]
[*]A DirectX 11-capable GPU[/*]
[*]Borderless/windowed mode for frame generation or Neural Rendering[/*]
[/list]

[b]My tested baseline is Skyrim SE 1.5.97.[/b] I have also tested the current GOG Skyrim Anniversary Edition 1.6.1170. Other runtime and mod combinations need their own validation; build support alone is not a compatibility guarantee.

[color=#f1c232]Check the Requirements and Files sections for the exact runtime/dependency information for the version you're downloading. SKSE and Engine Fixes are separate dependencies, not bundled replacements.[/color]

[line]
[size=4][b]INSTALLATION[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Back up saves and close Skyrim.[/*]
[*]Install matching SKSE and Engine Fixes prerequisites.[/*]
[*]Install PIXL Renderer with [b]MO2 or Vortex[/b] as a normal Data mod. For manual installation, extract the archive contents into Skyrim's [b]Data[/b] directory.[/*]
[*]Enable PIXL-TerrainField.esp and disable duplicate or conflicting engine-level renderers.[/*]
[*]Launch Skyrim through your usual [b]SKSE/mod-manager shortcut[/b].[/*]
[*]Complete [b]Quick Setup[/b]: choose your reconstruction path and quality profile, and optionally enable frame generation.[/*]
[*]If a restart is requested, save your game, exit and relaunch normally.[/*]
[*]Press [b]Page Down[/b] for PIXL Renderer and [b]Home[/b] for Photo Mode.[/*]
[/list]

The release includes a preloaded pipeline library. Additional permutations can still compile for a specific setup; allow compilation to finish before judging performance.

[b]The setup exit option saves PIXL settings, not your game progress.[/b] It requires confirmation and does not automatically relaunch Skyrim.

The release starts with my tuned fog and material settings. Reconstruction is set to Off/None, with frame generation and real-time Neural Rendering off until you choose to enable them. Accepting the existing quality selection preserves the tuned look.

[b]Shader cache[/b]

The release includes a preloaded pipeline library. Additional or invalidated permutations may still compile for your setup.

Let compilation finish before judging performance or visuals. Don't benchmark while shaders are compiling, and don't routinely delete a healthy cache. Normal module updates are designed to preserve unaffected cached stages.

[b]Updating or testing fresh defaults[/b]

Update with Skyrim closed. Existing user settings take precedence over new defaults.

To test the shipped defaults, back up [b]Data/SKSE/Plugins/PIXL/Config/UserGraphics.json[/b] outside the game directory, then remove the live copy while Skyrim is closed. The release archive does not include this file.

With MO2, check the active profile's mod/Overwrite location rather than assuming the file is physically in the game's Data folder.

[line]
[size=4][b]COMPATIBILITY[/b][/size]

PIXL expects to control Skyrim's engine-level shader pipeline.

[color=#f1c232][b]Do not stack this release with:[/b][/color]

[list]
[*]ENB.[/*]
[*]Community Shaders or another engine-level shader-hook renderer.[/*]
[*]Kreate.[/*]
[*]A second PIXL Renderer installation.[/*]
[/list]
[b]ReShade compatibility is untested and unsupported for this release.[/b] Please leave it disabled when testing or reporting PIXL issues.

With a modding ecosystem the size of Skyrim's, there will be plenty of combinations I haven't tested. Custom meshes, materials, weather mods and other rendering changes can affect the result.

[line]
[size=4][b]PERFORMANCE[/b][/size]

PIXL can be demanding. Use the Fast, Balanced, Enhanced and Cinematic quality profiles first, then adjust individual settings. Cinematic is intended for stronger systems and photo work. PIXL includes profiler and benchmarking tools for identifying expensive systems.

[img width=645]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/1704/images/189836/189836-1789150744-292083917.png[/img]

[line]
[size=4][b]PROJECT STATUS AND REPORTING[/b][/size]

This is a personal project that I will improve when time allows rather than a promise of a fixed update schedule. When reporting an issue, include the Skyrim runtime, PIXL version, GPU and driver, reconstruction/frame-generation settings, location/weather/time, reproduction steps, relevant logs and involved mods. Please remove personal information from logs before sharing them.

